        "behaviour": [
          "Keep Choose, Design and Connect. Add all five supported element types through the focused composer with an explicit destination, pending preview and retained input on refusal.",
          "Keep canvas, hierarchy and ancestor selection synchronized; show element type, nesting level and identifiable repeated containers.",
          "Edit text through an explicit action, Enter or double-click. Retain per-element drafts across selection changes; Apply and Cancel are explicit.",
          "Reorder siblings using buttons, Alt+arrows or pointer drag. Move groups with descendants; preserve source-only boundaries and selected identity.",
          "Every eligible removal opens a centered modal naming the element or listing the group descendants before any mutation. The background geometry and scroll position stay fixed.",
          "Focus Cancel initially; keep Tab within the dialog. Cancel or Escape changes neither source nor history and returns focus to the invoking control without scrolling.",
          "Confirm one removal as one history entry. Select and focus the next sibling, else previous sibling, else parent. Undo restores the exact subtree and selected target; Redo restores the fallback.",
          "Place Undo removal feedback outside the panel layout. Ignore repeated Delete and Backspace keydowns. Refuse screen-root removal, protected source and groups containing it.",
          "Retain pending input and source on invalid operations or source conflicts. Preserve compact navigation between editing and canvas."
        ],
        "deviations": [
          "Browser prototype uses fictional data and memory-only history. Sample Source is illustrative; real source patching, reconciliation, durable reopening and Ren'Py rendering remain implementation acceptance requirements.",
          "Connect explains the sample action only; action editing is outside #37 composition scope."
        ]
      }
